    <string name="wl_242" formatted="false">"Date, time and time zone come from the phone. System font. The watermark is embedded in photos and videos; changes apply to the next capture. Watermark is unavailable in HS: choose normal video mode."</string>
    <string name="wl_243" formatted="false">"How to use"</string>
    <string name="wl_244" formatted="false">"1. Install WristLens on your phone and paired watch. On first phone launch, allow camera, microphone and notifications. Opening the watch app then requests camera startup automatically. Android may require you to unlock the phone."</string>
    <string name="wl_245" formatted="false">"2. The central button takes a photo or starts video in the selected mode. Hold it in photo mode for a burst; release to stop. Maximum: 50 photos and 60 seconds after the first frame."</string>
    <string name="wl_246" formatted="false">"3. Bottom left switches photo/video, or pauses/resumes while recording. Bottom right opens the menu, or stops recording. Hold Stop to open the menu during recording."</string>
    <string name="wl_247" formatted="false">"4. Top buttons: flash, timer, switch camera. Tap the image for point focus. Use the rotating bezel/crown or camera settings to zoom."</string>
    <string name="wl_248" formatted="false">"5. Vibration for actions is a switch in the main menu. Only the camera screen stays awake; menus use the normal system screen timeout."</string>
    <string name="wl_249" formatted="false">"6. Photo and video timers are separate. Cancel a running timer with the central × button. Change resolution, FPS and format before recording. Only modes exposed to third-party Android apps are available."</string>
    <string name="wl_250" formatted="false">"7. Gallery supports a list with properties and two-column tiles. The counter includes the whole gallery. Hold a file, then Select all to include unloaded pages. Sharing supports up to 500 files per action; large deletions are processed in batches."</string>
    <string name="wl_251" formatted="false">"8. Camera settings includes background capture and watermark. Background capture keeps video and single timers running after leaving the watch app; a held burst always stops. Force stopping or restarting the phone interrupts capture."</string>
    <string name="wl_252" formatted="false">"9. Watermark supports four corners, black/white, three sizes, phone date and/or time. It is embedded in photos and videos and adds processing load. Turn it off for HS. Normal modes are checked at startup without silently reducing quality."</string>
    <string name="wl_253" formatted="false">"10. Disconnect on either device ends the session, saves recording and cancels timers, even with background capture enabled. Tap the phone button or reopen the watch app for a new session."</string>
    <string name="wl_254" formatted="false">"11. Defaults: DCIM/Camera, IMG/VID_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS, JPEG and MP4 H.264. On the watch, Files and saving contains phone originals and watch copies. On the phone, use File storage. Front screen flash requires the phone screen to stay open."</string>
